# Feature: KRA / KPI engine

## Weights
| KPI | Weight | Formula / source |
|---|---|---|
| On-time completion | 20% | Tasks completed by DueAt / completed tasks |
| Quality / approval | 20% | Approved output score / quality checklist |
| First-time right | 15% | Tasks approved without correction / eligible tasks |
| Correction performance | 10% | Weighted mistake corrections; improvements excluded |
| Creativity / design quality | 10% | Design Head/manual rating, controlled rubric |
| Cost control | 10% | Actual design cost vs approved estimate/standard |
| Team coordination | 5% | Dependency/hand-off compliance |
| Productivity | 5% | Standard hours vs actual active work hours |
| Documentation discipline | 5% | Required files, checklist, remarks completeness |

```
WeightedScore = SUM(MetricScore * WeightPercent / 100)
```

## Rules
- Recomputable from source events at any time.
- Store a `CalculationVersion` with every `EmployeeKpiScore` row so historical
  scores never silently change if the formula is revised later.
- Improvement-type corrections must be excluded from the Correction
  Performance metric (see `14-feature-correction.mdc`).

## Marks & grades
- Monthly recompute writes `EmployeePerformanceMark` (`KPI_MONTHLY`) and upserts
  `EmployeePerformanceGrade` for the UTC period.
- Grade bands (from weighted KPI 0–100): A ≥90, B ≥75, C ≥60, D ≥40, E below.
- Other mark sources: `DESIGN_CONTRIBUTION`, `CORRECTION_IMPACT`,
  `CREATIVITY_RATING`, `MANUAL_ADJUST`.
- `GET /api/kpi/employees` chart items include `gradeCode` + `marksBalance` for
  the current UTC month when a grade row exists.
- `GET /api/admin/employees` includes optional `gradeCode` + `marksBalance` for
  the current UTC month.
- `GET /api/kpi/employees/{id}/performance?year=&month=` returns grade, marks
  ledger, and live `marksBalance`.

## Design contribution
- `GET /api/designs/{id}/kpi-contribution` — per-contributor score breakdown on a design.
- `POST /api/designs/{id}/creativity-ratings` — Design Head creativity/design-quality
  rating (`employeeId`, `score`, optional `remark`); feeds creativity KPI + marks.

## Design Head rollups
Ideas created/completed by month, approved/rejected/live counts, average
development lead time, design-to-production and design-to-sales conversion,
team first-time-right/correction rate, department actual vs budget cost,
design success by season/collection/product type/target market.

## API
- `GET /api/kpi/employees`
- `GET /api/kpi/employees/{id}/performance`
- `GET /api/kpi/design-head`
- `POST /api/kpi/recompute`
- `GET /api/designs/{id}/kpi-contribution`
- `POST /api/designs/{id}/creativity-ratings`
